The '''president of Sinchew''' is the head of state of the [[Sinchew|Union of Sinchew, Hahkinawa and Mahik peoples]]. The office was established by the [[Constitution of Sinchew]] of 1733, and the first president was elected on 8 January 1736.

The president is elected by the [[General Assembly of Sinchew|General Assembly]], not by the population, and holds no mandate independent of the chamber that appoints him. The office conducts foreign affairs and administers the agencies the Assembly creates, and it is the civilian commander of the armed forces. It holds no domestic executive authority: the departments of state derive their authority from the Assembly, not from the president.

The presidential vote is the first business of the Assembly's second session in each term, and is held on 8 January. Terms are four years, with no limit on re-election, though most presidents of the early republic served one term.

