Three of the seven presidents held a given name from a tradition other than the one their surname belongs to, and three held Baiduist dharma names, the naming practice that had become near-universal among the Baiduist population after independence.

The first president, Ong Liongseng, served two terms and resigned midway through the second, in 1740, stating that he did not wish to hold the office indefinitely. He had also become ill, and he died a few months afterwards.

== Election ==

{{Main|General Assembly of Sinchew}}

The president is elected by the [[General Assembly of Sinchew|General Assembly]] by a majority of its members. The vote is taken as the first business of the Assembly's second session in each four-year term, which falls on 8 January.

The [[Constitution of Sinchew|constitution]] provides for no popular election of the president and no limit on re-election. The office is filled by the chamber whose agencies it administers, and its independence from that chamber is therefore limited to the two fields the constitution assigns it: foreign affairs, and the command of the armed forces.

== Powers ==

The office conducts foreign affairs and makes treaties without a ratification step. It is the civilian commander of the [[Armed Forces of Sinchew|armed forces]], though the Assembly raises, funds and may direct them. It administers the affairs of the agencies the Assembly creates, without commanding them.

It may declare martial law with the approval of the Assembly by a three-quarters majority - the only power in the constitution that the [[Senate of Sinchew|Senate]] does not gate.

